From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:19:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: USB
 controller as a mode switch

The QMP USB3-DP combo PHY stops the USB3 PIPE clock when DisplayPort
takes all four lanes (pin assignments C and E). Mark the controller
as a mode switch: it is the remote of the connector's high-speed
endpoint, so the Type-C mux state reaches it and it moves to the UTMI
clock before the PIPE clock goes, which keeps USB 2.0 working, e.g.
the hub of a USB-C monitor.

The connector then has three mode switches (the QMP PHY, the WCD939x
USB-SS switch and the controller), the most the Type-C class takes
(TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS).

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 5ed53e5b6547..cf5758dcba37 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -2489,6 +2489,13 @@
 	 */
 	/delete-property/ wakeup-source;
 
+	/*
+	 * With DisplayPort on all four lanes the QMP PHY stops the USB3 PIPE
+	 * clock; as a mode switch the controller moves to the UTMI clock first
+	 * and keeps USB 2.0 running (the hub of a USB-C monitor).
+	 */
+	mode-switch;
+
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
